<section data-expansion style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="narrow">
<h2 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(34px,4vw,52px);margin:0 0 28px;max-width:860px">How we earn links that help, and remove links that hurt</h2>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">Links from other sites tell search engines that a store is worth trusting. The right links come from sites your buyers already read. The wrong links, from unrelated or low-quality sites, can hold a store back.</p>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">What we do</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 26px;padding-left:22px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--ink2)"><li style="margin:0 0 8px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Audit.</strong> We review every site that links to your store, and identify the ones that are unrelated, low quality or harmful.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Clean up.</strong> Where harmful links are a real problem, we document them and submit a removal request to search engines.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Earn.</strong> We find relevant publications, industry blogs and directories where your buyers spend time, and create content or expert contributions that give those sites a reason to link.</li></ul>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">What we won't do</p>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">We don't buy links, use link networks or promise a number of links. Those methods can damage a store, and they don't last. Every link we build comes from a real relationship with a relevant site.</p>
<h3 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(32px,3.6vw,44px);margin:56px 0 24px">Frequently asked questions</h3>
<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--ink);margin:0 0 20px"><details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px 0"><summary style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer">How long do links take to show results?</summary><p class="p" style="margin:14px 0 0">Some take weeks to be published and indexed. Others take months to build trust. We report progress honestly, including the links that didn't happen.</p></details><details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px 0"><summary style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer">Do we need to approve each link?</summary><p class="p" style="margin:14px 0 0">Yes. You see every site we contact and every piece of content we propose before it goes out.</p></details></div>
</div></section>
